KZ2 patch 6046 (ENHANCEMENT): native mouse look, runtime side: Raw Input counts and the in-play pointer clip.

Adapted from Project Helghast, the Killzone 3 PC port (same author, MIT licence): its patches 2069 (native mouse look),
2097 (cursor hide and mouse lock) and 2123 (mouse feed on the window thread), libs/input/pad_mouse.{h,c}. Cut down to
what Killzone 2 uses: no menu pointer, no game-clock feed, no late latch.

libs/input/pad_mouse.{h,c}: WM_INPUT counts (relative, unaccelerated, unsmoothed) summed on the window thread and taken
once per look update by the game glue (port/kz2/kz2_ppu_overrides.cpp). Counts are kept only while the game is in play
(a look update took counts in the last 300 ms) and the window has the focus, so motion made in a menu or another window
never reaches the view. The pointer is clipped to the client area while focused and in play, released in menus, on focus
loss, minimise, a title-bar drag or resize, and on close (pad_mouse_tick from the window thread's loop, every <= 50 ms).
Mouse buttons stay keybinds (Mouse1 fire, Mouse2 zoom by default, as Project Helghast). KZ2_MOUSE_SCRIPT test input
(pure parser, host test tools/runtime/test_mouse_look.sh) and pad_mouse_send (SendInput, the full WM_INPUT path).

